  "notes": "\"Lowest drum aggression in the section\" is a claim about a number, and it is the number this file is built around: `velocityTiers.main` 64–78 and `accent` capped at 102, softer than every other entry in this batch including A Tribe Called Quest. The kit is brushed rather than cracked — ghost probability 0.34 against a low ghost velocity, hat velocities peaking at 0.7, and a ride lane carrying the wash from the source break. The harmony is the real bebop of the section: `ninth` at 0.42, the highest here, `triad` at 0.1, the lowest, genuine ii–V motion in both minor and major, and an i–VI–ii–V turnaround family. `super_locrian` is in the scale set at weight 1 for the altered-dominant colour the research names — it is the only entry in this batch that gets it, and it should stay rare. The upright bass walks in quarters and is \"very prominent\", so `followRootsProb` is 0.3 — the lowest in this batch — over a two-octave register with seven passing tones. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high: there is a first-person retrospective interview, but the tempo band and drum velocities are read from the records. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 52 to 49 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 50 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 3.",
